# FINAL-HAMILTONIAN CONTRACT (2026-11-08; source audit, not a new run)
# SM/QYM/QED/QG/NS: H = dGamma(h) = sum h_ij Cdag(e_i) A(e_j),
# creation LEFT, outer annihilation RIGHT. Keep all inner interactions in h.
# QG record: R^2 vielbein/TEGR, full exponential, no Taylor approximation.
# Spatial-derivative products use momentum convolution for NS/QG ONLY.
# H Omega = 0 is structural; ground status needs h >= 0. A gap above the
# unique outer vacuum needs an absolute h >= m I, m > 0, on the entire inner space.
# dGamma(h+c I) = H+c N_out; a chosen shift changes the occupied sectors.
# dGamma(B^2) generally differs from dGamma(B)^2 (cross-particle terms).
# Symbolic checks do not discharge physical identification or operator domains.
# SM comparison/inner derivation. General product Fourier checks
# do not extend the NS/QG-only spatial-derivative elimination work order.
# See docs/VERIFY_NESTED_FOCK_ENCLOSURE.md for scope and pending checks.
# Existing expression handles and stdout markers retain their extraction role.

# ======================================================================
# SM SOURCE AUDIT (2026-11-09; runtime validation pending)
# Reference: book.tex, "Majorana spinors in the Standard Model".
# This module checks scalar/CCR/CAR algebra and sector templates. It does
# NOT derive all chiral matrices, the full operator domain, or its ESA.
# Final object: H_SM=dGamma(h_SM), retaining all inner terms and constants.
# The exact full operator, not a simplified benchmark, is the required input
# to physical Hashimoto-SIRK validation (docs/SM_HAMILTONIAN_AUDIT.md).
#
# h_SM includes all gauge/Higgs terms, spatial Dirac derivative, operator-valued
# gauge-matter couplings and all four real Higgs/Yukawa components. The live
# bosonic comparison is 2 h_B + sum_active q^2 + c, not the legacy N_0.
# CHECK 8/12 are ordering identities for INNER comparison operators; scalar
# deletion is not required for outer-vacuum annihilation and quartic Wick
# sorting discards additional operator-valued contractions in the legacy CAS.
# CHECK 9 now retains distinct gauge, Higgs kinetic/covariant, Dirac and
# Yukawa slots. CHECK 11 is a U(1) Legendre normalization, not a scalar tautology.
# New checks probe Higgs normalization/constant and omitted sector entries.
# These changes need fresh engine/extraction checks. Old transcripts remain
# historical evidence only. No nonabelian BRST, physical reduction, full
# chiral matter assembly or Hashimoto error bound is proved by scalar templates.
# Run: cadabra2-cli -q -n docs/sm_gauge_fixed_hamiltonian.cdb
# ======================================================================

# ===========================================================================
# declarations
# ===========================================================================
{i1,i2,i3,i#,j#,k#,l#}::Indices(spatial,position=independent).
\epsilon_{i j k}::EpsilonTensor.
\partial{#}::PartialDerivative.
A_{k}::Depends(\partial{#}).
{pi0, pia, Bia, gcn, mu2, lam, xvar, phidphi}::Symbol.
{yuk, yukbar, phic, phis, bilin}::Symbol.
{inv2lam, ciso}::Symbol.
# (the Fock operators are bos/bosd and the CAR pair psi/psid — bare names
#  chosen to avoid colliding with the structure constants f_{abc} and the
#  index names a, b, c below)
{bos, bosd}::NonCommuting.
{psi, psid}::SelfAntiCommuting.
{psi, psid}::NonCommuting.
{a, b, c, a#, b#, c#}::Indices(frame,position=independent).

# ===========================================================================
# (1) the Weyl-gauge Legendre transform of one gauge family
#     (the yang_mills_hamiltonian.cdb identity, wired to the derived H)
# ===========================================================================
Lfam := (1/2) pia*pia - (1/2) Bia*Bia.
Hfam := pia*pia - @(Lfam).
distribute(Hfam)
canonicalise(Hfam)
hfinal = Hfam.copy()
htarget := (1/2) pia*pia + (1/2) Bia*Bia.
hcheck := @(hfinal) - @(htarget).
distribute(hcheck)
sort_product(hcheck)
canonicalise(hcheck)
collect_terms(hcheck)
print("CHECK 1  SMGF H_family = 1/2 pi^2 + 1/2 B^2 (Weyl Legendre)    (0 = ok):", hcheck);

# ===========================================================================
# (2) the abelian magnetic field: B_i = eps_{ijk} d_j A_k
#     The definition B_i = (1/2) eps_{ijk} (d_j A_k - d_k A_j) reduces to
#     the curl by the antisymmetry of eps and dummy renaming.
# ===========================================================================
bdef := (1/2) \epsilon_{i j k} \partial_{j}{A_{k}} - (1/2) \epsilon_{i j k} \partial_{k}{A_{j}}.
bcurl := \epsilon_{i j k} \partial_{j}{A_{k}}.
bchk := @(bdef) - @(bcurl).
distribute(bchk)
canonicalise(bchk)
collect_terms(bchk)
print("CHECK 2  SMGF B_i = (1/2) eps(dA - dA) = eps dA  (abelian curl) (0 = ok):", bchk);

# ===========================================================================
# (3) the non-abelian assembly: B_{i c} = (1/2) eps_{ijk} (d_j A_{k c}
#     - d_k A_{j c} + g f_{c b a} A_j^b A_k^a); the g f A A term vanishes
#     for g = 0, so the field must reduce to CHECK 2's curl there.
# ===========================================================================
A_{k c}::Depends(\partial{#}).
bnonab := (1/2) \epsilon_{i j k} ( \partial_{j}{A_{k c}} - \partial_{k}{A_{j c}} ) + (1/2)*gcn*\epsilon_{i j k} f_{c b a} A_{j b} A_{k a}.
bcurlc := \epsilon_{i j k} \partial_{j}{A_{k c}}.
bsub := @(bnonab).
substitute(bsub, $ gcn -> 0 $, repeat=True)
distribute(bsub)
canonicalise(bsub)
collect_terms(bsub)
bchk3 := @(bsub) - @(bcurlc).
distribute(bchk3)
canonicalise(bchk3)
collect_terms(bchk3)
print("CHECK 3  SMGF B_ic(g f A A) -> eps dA at g = 0  (non-abelian)  (0 = ok):", bchk3);

# ===========================================================================
# (4) the Higgs completed square:
#     4 lam V = -4 lam mu^2 x + 4 lam^2 x^2,
#     (2 lam x - mu^2)^2 - mu^4 = 4 lam^2 x^2 - 4 lam mu^2 x,
#     so 4 lam V + mu^4 = (2 lam x - mu^2)^2  at the level of assemblies.
#     The binomial is opened by explicit substitution (this build's
#     expand() does not open a polynomial power of a sum — the
#     mass_gap_norm_residual.cdb engine note).
# ===========================================================================
Vh := -mu2*phidphi + lam*phidphi*phidphi.
sqform := (2*lam*phidphi - mu2)**2.
substitute(sqform, $ (2*lam*phidphi - mu2)**2 -> 4*lam*lam*phidphi*phidphi - 4*lam*mu2*phidphi + mu2*mu2 $, repeat=True)
distribute(sqform)
canonicalise(sqform)
collect_terms(sqform)
hchk4 := 4*lam*@(Vh) + mu2*mu2 - @(sqform).
distribute(hchk4)
sort_product(hchk4)
canonicalise(hchk4)
collect_terms(hchk4)
print("CHECK 4  SMGF 4 lam V + mu^4 = (2 lam x - mu^2)^2  (Mexican hat) (0 = ok):", hchk4);

# ===========================================================================
# (5) the stationary point: dV/dx = -mu^2 + 2 lam x = 0 at x = mu^2/(2 lam).
#     x* is written mu2*inv2lam with the auxiliary symbol inv2lam =
#     (2 lam)^(-1); the rule 2*lam*inv2lam -> 1 is the definition.
# ===========================================================================
dVdx := -mu2 + 2*lam*phidphi.
dVsub := @(dVdx).
substitute(dVsub, $ phidphi -> mu2*inv2lam $, repeat=True)
distribute(dVsub)
collect_factors(dVsub)
# (substitute rules cannot carry a numerical prefactor on the lhs — so the
#  rule is on lam*inv2lam and the factor 2 stays outside)
substitute(dVsub, $ lam*inv2lam -> (1/2) $, repeat=True)
canonicalise(dVsub)
collect_terms(dVsub)
print("CHECK 5  SMGF dV/dx = 0 at x = mu^2/(2 lam)  (Higgs minimum)  (0 = ok):", dVsub);

# ===========================================================================
# (6) the Yukawa h.c. pairing: h_Y = y phi psibar psi + h.c.
#     Assembled as y*phi*bilin + ybar*phis*bilin; its Hermitian conjugate
#     swaps y <-> ybar and phi <-> phis.  The assembly must equal its own
#     conjugate (the +h.c. is what makes the Yukawa Hamiltonian Hermitian).
# ===========================================================================
hy := yuk*phic*bilin + yukbar*phis*bilin.
hydag := yukbar*phis*bilin + yuk*phic*bilin.
ychk := @(hy) - @(hydag).
distribute(ychk)
sort_product(ychk)
canonicalise(ychk)
collect_terms(ychk)
print("CHECK 6  SMGF h_Yukawa = h_Yukawa^dag  (h.c. pairing)          (0 = ok):", ychk);

# ===========================================================================
# (7) the CAR normalization of the Weyl fermions:
#     {psi, psi^dag} = psi psi^dag + psi^dag psi = 1.
# ===========================================================================
carchk := psi*psid + psid*psi - 1.
substitute(carchk, $ psi*psid -> 1 - psid*psi $, repeat=True)
distribute(carchk)
canonicalise(carchk)
collect_terms(carchk)
print("CHECK 7  SMGF psi psi^dag + psi^dag psi = 1  (CAR algebra)    (0 = ok):", carchk);

# ===========================================================================
# (8) INNER quadratic ordering identity. The shifted/Wick comparison differs
# from the specified inner operator. Outer H Omega=0 follows from enclosure
# without deleting this constant. Quartics require all contraction branches.
# ===========================================================================
uexp := (bosd + bos)*(bosd + bos).
distribute(uexp)
substitute(uexp, $ bos bosd -> bosd bos + 1 $, repeat=True)
distribute(uexp)
canonicalise(uexp)
hnorm := @(uexp) - 1.
hnchk := @(hnorm) - (bosd*bosd + 2*bosd*bos + bos*bos).
distribute(hnchk)
canonicalise(hnchk)
collect_terms(hnchk)
print("CHECK 8  SMGF u^2 = :u^2: + 1, inner Wick comparison (not outer vacuum)  (0 = ok):", hnchk);

# ===========================================================================
# (9) the assembled SM Hamiltonian:
#     H_SM = sum_X (1/2 pi_X^2 + 1/2 B_X^2) + |D phi|^2 + V(phi)
#            + h_Dirac + h_Yukawa.
#     Checked as an identity of assemblies: the sum of the sector
#     pieces equals the typed full form.
# ===========================================================================
# Scalar slots for one representative component of each sector. The actual
# multiplicities and chiral/generation matrices must be supplied separately.
{pGlu, pWeak, pHyp, bGlu, bWeak, bHyp, pHig, dHig, hDir}::Symbol.
gluonpart := (1/2) pGlu*pGlu + (1/2) bGlu*bGlu.
weakpart := (1/2) pWeak*pWeak + (1/2) bWeak*bWeak.
hyperpart := (1/2) pHyp*pHyp + (1/2) bHyp*bHyp.
higgskin := (1/2) pHig*pHig + (1/2) dHig*dHig.
Hsm := (1/2) pGlu*pGlu + (1/2) bGlu*bGlu
      + (1/2) pWeak*pWeak + (1/2) bWeak*bWeak
      + (1/2) pHyp*pHyp + (1/2) bHyp*bHyp
      + (1/2) pHig*pHig + (1/2) dHig*dHig
      - mu2*phidphi + lam*phidphi*phidphi + hDir
      + yuk*phic*bilin + yukbar*phis*bilin.
Hsectors := @(gluonpart) + @(weakpart) + @(hyperpart) + @(higgskin)
           + @(Vh) + hDir + @(hy).
aschk := @(Hsm) - @(Hsectors).
distribute(aschk)
sort_product(aschk)
canonicalise(aschk)
collect_terms(aschk)
print("CHECK 9  SMGF H_SM = sum sectors  (assembly)                   (0 = ok):", aschk);

# ===========================================================================
# (10) the BRST charge assembly: G_SM = G_G + G_W + G_B, with the U(1)
#      factor's abelian limit G_B = c^j d_j pi^j (no f A pi term).
#      The non-abelian family charge is the yang_mills_hamiltonian.cdb
#      G_y form; at g = 0 (f -> 0) it must reduce to the abelian one.
# ===========================================================================
{j,k,l,j#,k#,l#}::Indices(frame,position=independent).
{c^{j}, b_{j}}::SelfAntiCommuting.
{c^{j}, b_{j}}::NonCommuting.
{A_{\mu?}^{j}, \pi^{\mu?}_{j}}::NonCommuting.
i::ImaginaryI.
Gy := c^{j} D_{j l \mu} \pi^{\mu l} + c^{j} f_{j k}^{l} A_{\mu}^{k} \pi^{\mu l} + (1/2) i f_{j k}^{l} c^{j} c^{k} b_{l}.
Gabel := c^{j} D_{j l \mu} \pi^{\mu l}.
gsub := @(Gy).
substitute(gsub, $ f_{j k}^{l} -> 0 $, repeat=True)
distribute(gsub)
canonicalise(gsub)
gchk := @(gsub) - @(Gabel).
distribute(gchk)
canonicalise(gchk)
collect_terms(gchk)
print("CHECK 10 SMGF G_SM(f->0) = c d pi  (BRST assembly, abelian)   (0 = ok):", gchk);

# ===========================================================================
# (11) U(1) Legendre normalization, independently assembled.
# This fixes the electric/magnetic coefficient in this scalar template;
# it does not establish physical hypercharges or the matter representation.
# ===========================================================================
uoneL := (1/2) pHyp*pHyp - (1/2) bHyp*bHyp.
uoneH := pHyp*pHyp - @(uoneL).
symchk := @(uoneH) - ((1/2) pHyp*pHyp + (1/2) bHyp*bHyp).
distribute(symchk)
canonicalise(symchk)
collect_terms(symchk)
print("CHECK 11 SMGF U(1) Legendre electric/magnetic coefficients (0 = ok):", symchk);

# ===========================================================================
# (12) the fermionic normal-ordering strip: psi psi^dag normal-orders to
#      :psi psi^dag: = -psi^dag psi plus the scalar +1, and THAT scalar
#      labels a shifted inner comparison, not the physical outer vacuum.
#      Checked content: psi psi^dag - (-psi^dag psi) - 1 = 0, i.e. the
#      stripped constant is exactly 1 (the fermionic zero-point).
# ===========================================================================
fchk := psi*psid - ( - psid*psi ) - 1.
substitute(fchk, $ psi*psid -> 1 - psid*psi $, repeat=True)
distribute(fchk)
canonicalise(fchk)
collect_terms(fchk)
print("CHECK 12 SMGF psi psi^dag = -psi^dag psi + 1, scalar stripped  (0 = ok):", fchk);

# ===========================================================================
# (13) the UNBROKEN <-> BROKEN shift identity.  The unbroken potential
#      V = -mu^2 x + lam x^2 (CHECK 4, the Mexican hat) written around the
#      condensate: x = (v + h)^2 / 2 at the minimum mu^2 = lam v^2 gives
#        V = -lam v^4/4 + lam v^2 h^2 + lam v h^3 + (lam/4) h^4,
#      i.e. the constant vacuum energy, the radial-mode (Higgs) mass term,
#      and the cubic + quartic self-couplings — the SAME function, no
#      approximation.  The binomials are opened by explicit substitution
#      (this build's expand() does not open a polynomial power of a sum).
# ===========================================================================
{vsh, hsh}::Symbol.
xshift := (1/2)*(vsh + hsh)**2.
substitute(xshift, $ (vsh + hsh)**2 -> vsh*vsh + 2*vsh*hsh + hsh*hsh $, repeat=True)
distribute(xshift)
canonicalise(xshift)
collect_terms(xshift)
Vshift := -mu2*@(xshift) + lam*@(xshift)*@(xshift).
substitute(Vshift, $ mu2 -> lam*vsh*vsh $, repeat=True)
distribute(Vshift)
canonicalise(Vshift)
collect_terms(Vshift)
Vtarget := -(1/4)*lam*vsh*vsh*vsh*vsh + lam*vsh*vsh*hsh*hsh + lam*vsh*hsh*hsh*hsh + (1/4)*lam*hsh*hsh*hsh*hsh.
chk13 := @(Vshift) - @(Vtarget).
distribute(chk13)
collect_factors(chk13)
sort_product(chk13)
canonicalise(chk13)
collect_terms(chk13)
print("CHECK 13 SMGF V(broken form) - (-lam v^4/4 + lam v^2 h^2 + lam v h^3 + lam h^4/4) (0 = ok):", chk13);

# ===========================================================================
# (14) the radial-mode (Higgs) mass, assembled two ways:
#      route 1: the quadratic coefficient of CHECK 13 is lam v^2, and
#        V = ... + (1/2) m_h^2 h^2 + ...  =>  m_h^2 = 2 lam v^2;
#      route 2: V''(x) at the minimum: d2V = -mu^2 + 6 lam x at
#        x = v^2/2, mu^2 = lam v^2  =>  m_h^2 = 2 lam v^2.
# ===========================================================================
d2V := -mu2 + 6*lam*xvar.
substitute(d2V, $ xvar -> (1/2)*vsh*vsh $, repeat=True)
substitute(d2V, $ mu2 -> lam*vsh*vsh $, repeat=True)
distribute(d2V)
collect_factors(d2V)
sort_product(d2V)
canonicalise(d2V)
collect_terms(d2V)
chk14 := @(d2V) - 2*lam*vsh*vsh.
distribute(chk14)
collect_factors(chk14)
sort_product(chk14)
canonicalise(chk14)
collect_terms(chk14)
print("CHECK 14 SMGF m_h^2 = 2 lam v^2 (coefficient vs V''(v))       (0 = ok):", chk14);

# (15-17) Convention and omission probes. Executed 2026-11-09c.
{rsqSM, vevSM}::Symbol.
realpot := -(1/2) mu2*rsqSM + (1/4) lam*rsqSM*rsqSM.
doubletpot = Vh.copy()
substitute(doubletpot, $ phidphi -> (1/2) rsqSM $, repeat=True)
realnormcheck := @(doubletpot) - @(realpot).
distribute(realnormcheck)
collect_terms(realnormcheck)
print("CHECK 15 SMGF phi^dag phi = sum real phi_a^2/2 (expect 0):", realnormcheck)
if str(realnormcheck) != "0":
    raise AssertionError("SMGF Higgs real/doublet normalization mismatch")
positivewall := (1/4) lam*(rsqSM - vevSM*vevSM)*(rsqSM - vevSM*vevSM).
constantcheck := @(positivewall) - @(realpot) - (1/4) lam*vevSM*vevSM*vevSM*vevSM.
substitute(constantcheck, $ mu2 -> lam*vevSM*vevSM $, repeat=True)
distribute(constantcheck)
sort_product(constantcheck)
canonicalise(constantcheck)
collect_terms(constantcheck)
print("CHECK 16 SMGF fixed inner Higgs constant retained (expect 0):", constantcheck)
if str(constantcheck) != "0":
    raise AssertionError("SMGF Higgs constant mismatch")
# Independently zero all unrelated sector slots to expose missing terms.
for label, slot in [("Dirac", "hDir"), ("Higgs momentum", "pHig"), ("Higgs covariant", "dHig")]:
    probed = Hsm.copy()
    substitute(probed, Ex("pGlu -> 0, bGlu -> 0, pWeak -> 0, bWeak -> 0, pHyp -> 0, bHyp -> 0, mu2 -> 0, lam -> 0, yuk -> 0, yukbar -> 0"), repeat=True)
    if slot == "hDir":
        substitute(probed, Ex("hDir -> 1, pHig -> 0, dHig -> 0"), repeat=True)
        expected = Ex("1")
    elif slot == "pHig":
        substitute(probed, Ex("hDir -> 0, pHig -> 1, dHig -> 0"), repeat=True)
        expected = Ex("1/2")
    else:
        substitute(probed, Ex("hDir -> 0, pHig -> 0, dHig -> 1"), repeat=True)
        expected = Ex("1/2")
    probecheck = Ex("("+str(probed)+")-("+str(expected)+")")
    distribute(probecheck)
    collect_terms(probecheck)
    print("CHECK 17 SMGF retained " + label + " coefficient (expect 0):", probecheck)
    if str(probecheck) != "0":
        raise AssertionError("SMGF missing " + label + " slot")
# The full four-component chiral Yukawa matrix identity is a separate P1/N2
# deliverable. No scalar placeholder is promoted to that physical identity.
